.TH http_sendreq 3 "HTTP Library Functions" "QuickJS" "HTTP Library Functions"

.SH NAME
http_sendreq \- Send an HTTP request

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/http.h>
.B int http_sendreq(http* h);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B http_sendreq function sends an HTTP request.

The function takes one parameter:
.I h
The HTTP structure.

The function returns 0 on success, or -1 on error.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B http_sendreq function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/http.h>

int main() {
  // Assume h is a valid HTTP structure
  http h;

  // Initialize h

  int ret = http_sendreq(&h);

  if (ret < 0) {
    perror("http_sendreq");
    return 1;
  }

  // Use the result

  return 0;
}
.!
